{"seq":1,"slug":"why-ai-friendly-architecture","title":"Why Ai Friendly Architecture","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-architecture/why-ai-friendly-architecture","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-changes-when-agents-code","title":"当 Agent 参与编码,什么变了","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-architecture/why-ai-friendly-architecture/what-changes-when-agents-code","wordCount":2270,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"ai-friendliness-as-design-goal","title":"把 AI 可理解可修改作为设计目标","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-architecture/why-ai-friendly-architecture/ai-friendliness-as-design-goal","wordCount":2417,"readingTime":10},{"seq":3,"slug":"human-and-agent-shared-codebase","title":"人与 Agent 共享的代码库","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-architecture/why-ai-friendly-architecture/human-and-agent-shared-codebase","wordCount":2183,"readingTime":9}],"introHtml":"<p>本章讲清为什么「AI 友好」值得成为一等的架构目标:当 agent 从「补全片段」走向「自主完成任务」,代码库被阅读和改动的方式发生了什么根本变化;为什么我们应当主动把「让 agent 易理解、易修改、改得安全」设为设计目标,而非被动适应;以及人与 agent 共享同一个代码库时,二者对架构的诉求为何高度同源——为 agent 优化的,几乎都是为人优化的。</p>\n"}